From: Amaral Adreno Tools
Subject: turnip: incorporate validated community stability fixes

Source: https://github.com/whitebelyash/mesa-unified/pull/12
Upstream commits reviewed:
  8b682bc176c7f595860255dd8266824fb411650d
  5375e79c92b93b61bb41abce8958dd0f34761edd
  fb1bee8541595f46f9ddf2507f8a3ee94e354f69
  20318c51998b3d4f9388b66302e370a458b8a3ac
  a06667fa8bdecd73d22fc27cb00b12d54fa734b2

This patch contains only correctness and resource-lifetime fixes:

* propagate command-stream allocation failure and release the pipeline object;
* avoid dereferencing a NULL BO for VK_NULL_HANDLE buffer bindings;
* release KGSL profiling command objects after queue submission;
* release derived performance counters when destroying their query pool;
* destroy shader variants when shader upload fails.

It deliberately excludes the duplicate MSAA register-emission optimization and
the latent suballocator hardening from the source pull request.

